    "Every invocation creates, seeds, and removes its own temporary database and local server. No real player data or public service is used.",
    "The same workload driver was copied into an isolated archive of the baseline commit; both builds used the same installed locked dependencies. Before and after runs were sequential.",
    "The API workload intentionally uses the unchanged legacy full-response wire format and the same requests, including duplicate mutation IDs. The browser workload measures the actual client, including opt-in compact responses and revalidation.",
    "Accelerated limits apply only to benchmark workers; public limit behavior is covered by separate tests. There are 5000 synthetic completed records before measurement.",
    "Outcomes still use cryptographic randomness; small JSON/database-size variation is expected. Results are single local runs, not capacity, statistical confidence intervals, or multi-hour soak tests.",
    "API latency includes reading the full response on localhost. Request/response body counters exclude HTTP headers. CPU is for the child server; peak RSS is sampled every 20 ms and includes a final sample after query profiling.",
    "Chrome encoded response counts include response headers and compressed bytes, but exclude request headers. Decoded body bytes are also recorded. Browser-level request/latency counters at the top of browser reports are zero because the driver measures browser traffic separately.",
    "Compaction and offline VACUUM occur after timing the repeated workload. They retain all receipt IDs, fingerprints, and full original responses; the maintenance report is a separate repeated run."
